 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in Senate",
   "date": "2019-05-15",
   "text": "Protect Drinking Water from PFAS Act of 2019\n This bill requires the Environmental Protection Agency to issue a maximum contaminant level goal as well as a national primary drinking water regulation for certain perfluoroalkyl and polyfluoroalkyl substances, commonly referred to as PFAS. The substances are man-made and may have adverse human health effects. A variety of products contain PFAS, such as nonstick cookware or weatherproof clothing."
  }
